    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Owen Reilly is delighted to present this unique one-bedroom plus mezzanine apartment situated on the top floor of St Kevin’s Church built c. 1883 by by Sir Thomas Drew in a Gothic Revival style and converted in 1994 into residential apartments. Located in the heart of Portobello on Bloomfield Avenue just off the South Circular Road. Features include original architraves and special feature arched window with stained glass in the living room, and vaulted timber ceilings giving abundance of character. The accommodation briefly comprises entrance hall, living/dining, kitchen, double bedroom, and a stunning mezzanine level providing additional flexible accommodation and a shower room.  The property also comes with a secure, designated parking space located behind security gates and a secure bicycle storage area.\r\n\r\nNotably, Saint Kevin's stands as Ireland's first church-to-apartment conversion, with architect Mary Donohoe playing a key role in ensuring its architectural heritage remained central to the design—such as preserving the large Gothic window some units. Adjacent to the apartments, the original church hall was converted into a community centre, officially opening in 1995 after a refurbishment led by St Kevin’s Community Council. It has served Portobello residents ever since, reinforcing the building’s dual role in both residential and civic life.\r\n\r\nMore about this location...\r\n\r\nLocated in in one of Dublin’s most sought after locations adjacent to the Grand Canal in Portobello, a host of amenities on the doorstep of Camden Street with its hip cafes, restaurants, bars, antique shops and boutiques, St Stephen’s Green and its shopping centre as well as Grafton street. The property is well serviced by public transport, within a 7-minute walk you can reach the Luas at Harcourt, the property is serviced by many buses including 9, 15, 15a, 15b, 16, 16D, 68, 68A, 69, 122, 140, 142, and E1. Must be viewed to be appreciated."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall\r\n(3.86m x 1.4m and 4.27m x 1.81m)\r\nA distinctive entrance hall with an impressive pitched ceiling, exposed timber beams and beautiful solid wood flooring, opening through to the inner hallway.\r\n\r\n\r\nLiving / Dining Room\r\n(8.15m x 3.51m)\r\nA truly exceptional reception space, centred around a dramatic double-height ceiling and two magnificent Gothic-style windows with inset glass. Exposed solid timber beams and solid wood flooring enhance the character and warmth of this remarkable room. A mezzanine level overlooks the living space, adding to its impressive sense of volume.\r\n\r\n\r\nKitchen\r\n(2.42m x 1.74m)\r\nA well-appointed kitchen featuring a range of built-in floor units, solid wood worktops, integrated electric oven and hob, stainless steel extractor fan and classic white subway tiled splashback. The pitched ceiling and exposed timber beams continue the property’s distinctive architectural style.\r\n\r\n\r\nShower Room\r\n(2m x 1.64m)\r\nA stylish shower room comprising a large walk-in shower enclosure, pedestal wash hand basin and WC. Finished with tiled flooring and extensively tiled walls in classic white subway tiles.\r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom\r\n(2.71m x 2.58m)\r\nA generous double bedroom with built-in wardrobes, Velux window, solid wood flooring and an attractive pitched ceiling with exposed timber beams.\r\n\r\nMezzanine\r\n(4.85m x 3m)\r\nA particularly striking additional living space overlooking the main reception room. Featuring a large Velux window, pitched ceiling and exposed timber beams, this versatile area makes the most of the property’s exceptional height and architectural character."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Unique apartment in a converted church.\r\nStunning living room with pitched ceilings.\r\nAmazing gothic features throughout.\r\nElectric heating.\r\nSought after location in Portobello.\r\nManagement charge c. €2,500 per annum.\r\nMinutes walk to Dublin city centre with all its amenities.\r\nDesignated Parking Space behind secure gates.\r\nWithin a 7-Minute walk to Luas at Harcourt."
      },
      {
